            <ArticleTitle>[Athrombogenic activity of endothelium in patients with cerebral complications of hypertensive disease and concomitant coronary heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study of antiaggregative and anticoagulant activities of endothelium included 90 patients with cerebral complications of hypertensive disease and coronary heart disease in the acute and early rehabilitation period after ischemic stroke. The study revealed paradoxical prothrombotic activity of endothelium and compromised antithrombotic potential of the vascular wall.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
